061 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257061 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257062 13194139533864 true] [17592186257061 1110 #uuid "1b400207-bef6-55aa-8972-5e014ca89499" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257062 1034 "-110" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257062 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257062 1111 #uuid "2c354b3b-46f8-52ed-b64b-3bd9ce8ee2eb" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257063 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257064 13194139533864 true] [17592186257063 1089 "q-123953" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257063 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186257063 1100 "Determine the third partial sum of the series\n${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{n}.$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257063 1113 #uuid "08572949-7072-5fd4-8efb-71e1ae8b0ef7" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257063 1145 "Let ${a}_{n}={(\\frac{3}{4})}^{n}.$ We note that this is a geometric sequence with $r=\\frac{3}{4}$ and first term given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}={(\\frac{3}{4})}^{1}=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nThe $k$th partial sum of a geometric series is given by\n\n$$\n{s}_{k}={a}_{1}(\\frac{1-{r}^{k}}{1-r}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the third partial sum is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}_{3}={\\sum }_{n=1}^{3}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot \\frac{(1-{r}^{3})}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot \\frac{(1-{[\\frac{3}{4}]}^{3})}{(1-\\frac{3}{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot \\frac{(1-\\frac{27}{64})}{(\\frac{1}{4})} \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\cancel{\\frac{1}{4}}\\cdot \\frac{(\\frac{37}{64})}{(\\cancel{\\frac{1}{4}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{111}{64}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257064 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257065 13194139533864 true] [17592186257064 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257064 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257064 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257065 13194139533864 true] [17592186257064 1110 #uuid "b47e73b7-93d8-592f-8c7f-093290c1c619" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257065 1034 "\\frac{111}{64}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257065 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257065 1111 #uuid "1dcbcdb3-5e2f-56b9-bcfa-9b3fa533e8a2" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257066 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257067 13194139533864 true] [17592186257066 1089 "q-123961" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257066 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533864 true] [17592186257066 1100 "Consider the series ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(-\\sqrt{3}).$ Does it converge or diverge? If it converges, what is the sum of the series?" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257066 1113 #uuid "743b96cc-15a3-5525-bc3d-b9c616d0fdc1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257066 1145 "Let's compute the first few partial sums:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}_{1} & =-\\sqrt{3} \\\\ {s}_{2} & =-\\sqrt{3}+(-\\sqrt{3})=-2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ {s}_{3} & =-\\sqrt{3}+(-\\sqrt{3})+(-\\sqrt{3})=-3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ {s}_{4} & =-\\sqrt{3}+(-\\sqrt{3})+(-\\sqrt{3})+(-\\sqrt{3})=-4\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the sequence of partial sums, we can see that the formula for the $n$th partial sum is \n\n$$\n{s}_{n}=-\\sqrt{3}n.\n$$\n\nThe sequence of partial sums is divergent:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{s}_{n}={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }(-\\sqrt{3}n)=-\\infty \n$$\n\nTherefore, the series ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(-\\sqrt{3})$ is also divergent." 13194139533864 true] [17592186257067 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257068 13194139533864 true] [17592186257067 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257069 13194139533864 true] [17592186257067 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533864 true] [17592186257067 1041 "selection" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257067 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257068 13194139533864 true] [17592186257067 1110 #uuid "97963b45-365e-5cfd-b622-26978b6bae07" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257068 1034 "Diverges" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257068 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257068 1111 #uuid "7b01190d-f335-5a2f-9c2f-a1d6a06a1693" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257069 1034 "Converges" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257069 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257069 1111 #uuid "75282ae4-fa28-5274-b61f-5ff217fb2b6f" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257070 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257071 13194139533864 true] [17592186257070 1089 "q-123969" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257070 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533864 true] [17592186257070 1100 "Consider the series ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\operatorname{sin}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ).$ Does it converge or diverge? If it converges, what is the sum of the series?" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257070 1113 #uuid "07ca5e2d-77a2-57ef-9113-ced1d4775a46" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257070 1145 "Let's compute the first few partial sums:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}_{1} & =\\operatorname{sin}(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})=-1 \\\\ {s}_{2} & =-1+\\operatorname{sin}(\\frac{5\\pi }{2})=0 \\\\ {s}_{3} & =0+\\operatorname{sin}(\\frac{7\\pi }{2})=-1 \\\\ {s}_{4} & =-1+\\operatorname{sin}(\\frac{9\\pi }{2})=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the above, we can see that the sequence of partial sums oscillates between $0$ and $-1$ forever. \n\nSo the limit of the sequence of partial sums does not exist, and therefore the series is divergent." 13194139533864 true] [17592186257071 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257072 13194139533864 true] [17592186257071 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257073 13194139533864 true] [17592186257071 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533864 true] [17592186257071 1041 "selection" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257071 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257072 13194139533864 true] [17592186257071 1110 #uuid "fc98c227-8f2c-5b60-8bb3-540c6f306dcc" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257072 1034 "Diverges" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257072 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257072 1111 #uuid "a66ce1c5-7ce5-5c02-afed-46f3d17ce2e7" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257073 1034 "Converges" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257073 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257073 1111 #uuid "522c1f8e-78bc-58fa-9df4-84520078285a" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257074 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257075 13194139533864 true] [17592186257074 1089 "q-124060" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257074 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186257074 1100 "Consider the series ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{n}{2}.$ Does it converge or diverge? If it converges, what is the sum of the series?" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257074 1113 #uuid "c556c0fb-0999-5d66-8c7d-1dbc40d7dbff" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257074 1145 "The given series is an arithmetic series. Its first term is\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2},\n$$\n\nand its $n$th term is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{n}{2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we get the following formula for the $n$th partial sum:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}_{n} & =\\frac{n}{2}({a}_{1}+{a}_{n}) \\\\  & =\\frac{n}{2}(\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{n}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{n(1+n)}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTaking the limit of the partial sums, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{s}_{n} & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{n(1+n)}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{n}^{2} \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since the limit of the sequence of partial sums is infinite, the series is divergent." 13194139533864 true] [17592186257075 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257076 13194139533864 true] [17592186257075 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257077 13194139533864 true] [17592186257075 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533864 true] [17592186257075 1041 "selection" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257075 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257076 13194139533864 true] [17592186257075 1110 #uuid "b69e70c1-efa4-5882-aa08-8ecc147d051d" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257076 1034 "Diverges" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257076 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257076 1111 #uuid "8d67d966-acfc-5538-936e-5bb90e6f6882" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257077 1034 "Converges" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257077 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257077 1111 #uuid "a3688785-1084-5422-8f3a-12fc901bf9f4" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257078 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257079 13194139533864 true] [17592186257078 1089 "q-124062" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257078 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533864 true] [17592186257078 1100 "Consider the series ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(n+3).$ Does it converge or diverge? If it converges, what is the sum of the series?" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257078 1113 #uuid "afd7d27e-c371-5649-a501-b00a45a6a8b4" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257078 1145 "The given series is an arithmetic series. Its first term is\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=1+3=4,\n$$\n\nIts $n$th term is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=n+3.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we get the following formula for the $n$th partial sum:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}_{n} & =\\frac{n}{2}({a}_{1}+{a}_{n}) \\\\  & =\\frac{n}{2}(4+n+3) \\\\  & =\\frac{n(7+n)}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTaking the limit of the partial sums, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{s}_{n} & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{n(7+n)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{n}^{2} \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since the limit of the sequence of partial sums is infinite, the series is divergent." 13194139533864 true] [17592186257079 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257080 13194139533864 true] [17592186257079 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257081 13194139533864 true] [17592186257079 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533864 true] [17592186257079 1041 "selection" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257079 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257080 13194139533864 true] [17592186257079 1110 #uuid "5291b67e-7185-5f08-96fc-2f36ec0b9d6d" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257080 1034 "Diverges" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257080 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257080 1111 #uuid "db8ae490-21a6-564a-8c12-32e6bd7fc5f5" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257081 1034 "Converges" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257081 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257081 1111 #uuid "16877732-d7c6-5ba5-a177-69fec44dad3f" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257082 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257083 13194139533864 true] [17592186257082 1089 "q-124064" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257082 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533864 true] [17592186257082 1100 "If ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}=-\\frac{3}{4}$, \nthen calculate ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }8{a}_{n}.$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257082 1113 #uuid "8c0a953b-56c6-5668-952a-c90e6b1ea708" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257082 1145 "Taking the constant factor outside of the summation sign gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }8{a}_{n} & =8{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n} \\\\  & =8(-\\frac{3}{4}) \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257083 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257084 13194139533864 true] [17592186257083 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257083 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257083 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257084 13194139533864 true] [17592186257083 1110 #uuid "83199529-9873-5d3d-9f07-29285488bb05" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257084 1034 "-6" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257084 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257084 1111 #uuid "42142022-6da5-5db6-96e0-957c33de6428" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257085 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257086 13194139533864 true] [17592186257085 1089 "q-124085" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257085 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186257085 1100 "Given that ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is divergent, which of the following statements is true regarding the series ${\\sum }_{n=k}^{\\infty }{a}_{n},$ where $k$ is a positive integer, and ${a}_{n}$ is well-defined for all $n⩾1?$\n\nI. - It is convergent for $1<k\\le 500$\nII. - It is divergent for $k>500$\nIII. - It is convergent for $50<k\\le 100$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257085 1113 #uuid "f70941eb-1b43-57e6-9bb7-b412bbea5880" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257085 1145 "Removing the first $k-1$ terms from a divergent series results in a divergent series.\n\nMore precisely, assume ${a}_{n}$ is well-defined for $n\\ge 1$ and $k\\ge 1$ is an integer. Then, we have the following:\n\n*If ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is divergent, then ${\\sum }_{n=k}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is also divergent.*\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257086 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257087 13194139533864 true] [17592186257086 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257088 13194139533864 true] [17592186257086 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257089 13194139533864 true] [17592186257086 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257090 13194139533864 true] [17592186257086 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257091 13194139533864 true] [17592186257086 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257092 13194139533864 true] [17592186257086 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257093 13194139533864 true] [17592186257086 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257094 13194139533864 true] [17592186257086 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533864 true] [17592186257086 1041 "selection" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257086 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257094 13194139533864 true] [17592186257086 1110 #uuid "d2d0d90d-66d3-54f5-a712-29e05a119d40" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257087 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257087 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257087 1111 #uuid "23e27595-0a81-5428-9abb-089c83c08a05" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257088 1034 "II and III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257088 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257088 1111 #uuid "9345163d-02cc-5438-87af-72f9c7ee5893" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257089 1034 "I and III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257089 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257089 1111 #uuid "1c66f9e1-7093-5248-babb-26644ce91839" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257090 1034 "I only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257090 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257090 1111 #uuid "3f944afb-cc01-513f-8688-1027dbd1a9e3" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257091 1034 "III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257091 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257091 1111 #uuid "b7ce0565-dbc7-52a4-b169-d172edd975cc" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257092 1034 "I and II only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257092 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257092 1111 #uuid "33220375-c9f2-51c0-b090-41092480c806" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257093 1034 "None of those listed" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257093 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257093 1111 #uuid "442a40ce-f652-5e35-8b50-d1e22420cb13" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257094 1034 "II only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257094 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257094 1111 #uuid "4ec4cb49-cedd-56c8-9b45-dc0e15e2bbd1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257095 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257096 13194139533864 true] [17592186257095 1089 "q-124086" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257095 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186257095 1100 "Given that ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent and ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is convergent, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. - $-{10}^{500}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent\nII. - ${\\sum }_{n=25}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is divergent\nIII. - ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}-{10}^{500}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is divergent" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257095 1113 #uuid "b0132ee2-97f1-5701-b78e-440561d08c8c" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257095 1145 "Let's recall the properties of convergent series:\n\n- If ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent, then ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }K\\cdot {a}_{n}=K\\cdot {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is also convergent.\n\n- If ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent and ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is convergent, then ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is convergent.\n\n- If ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent, then ${\\sum }_{n=k}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is also convergent.\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. Any constant multiple of a convergent series gives a convergent series.\n\n- Statement II is false. Removing a finite number of terms from a convergent series gives a convergent series.\n\n- Statement III is false. The sum of two convergent series is convergent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257096 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257097 13194139533864 true] [17592186257096 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257098 13194139533864 true] [17592186257096 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257099 13194139533864 true] [17592186257096 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257100 13194139533864 true] [17592186257096 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257101 13194139533864 true] [17592186257096 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257102 13194139533864 true] [17592186257096 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257103 13194139533864 true] [17592186257096 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257104 13194139533864 true] [17592186257096 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533864 true] [17592186257096 1041 "selection" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257096 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257100 13194139533864 true] [17592186257096 1110 #uuid "907ac348-0d31-53aa-a507-4f3224e0eb36" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257097 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257097 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257097 1111 #uuid "93784fbc-83fc-552e-bca4-b879f0cba48b" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257098 1034 "II and III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257098 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257098 1111 #uuid "39dc14bc-8f7b-5dc0-8c25-db4ce0daa200" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257099 1034 "I and III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257099 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257099 1111 #uuid "e8f6245f-990b-5cb6-ac0d-2f2ad6dedd8c" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257100 1034 "I only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257100 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257100 1111 #uuid "58f239de-e4fd-55ef-a60a-235d023bd6dc" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257101 1034 "III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257101 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257101 1111 #uuid "513ed02a-8b72-53e8-ab93-d7cda8f774bc" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257102 1034 "I and II only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257102 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257102 1111 #uuid "eb95d64c-4c75-5942-9e5f-6610b98a0140" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257103 1034 "None of those listed" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257103 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257103 1111 #uuid "5f45a70f-c513-545e-9bae-0dea0270c330" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257104 1034 "II only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257104 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257104 1111 #uuid "11df1ff9-b048-5c6b-afa7-e4921a4772e3" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257105 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257106 13194139533864 true] [17592186257105 1089 "q-124087" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257105 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186257105 1100 "Given that ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent and ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is convergent, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. - ${\\sum }_{n=100}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent\nII. - $-{10}^{10}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is convergent\nIII. - ${\\sum }_{n=100}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}-{10}^{10}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is convergent." 13194139533864 true] [17592186257105 1113 #uuid "a5033c15-e0ed-52f4-b026-2ec54fd36d33" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257105 1145 "Let's recall the properties of convergent series:\n\n- If ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent, then ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }K\\cdot {a}_{n}=K\\cdot {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is also convergent.\n\n- If ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent and ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is convergent, then ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is convergent.\n\n- If ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent, then ${\\sum }_{n=k}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is also convergent.\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. Removing a finite number of terms from a convergent series gives a convergent series.\n\n- Statement II is true. Any constant multiple of a convergent series gives a convergent series.\n\n- Statement III is true. The sum of two convergent series is convergent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257106 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257107 13194139533864 true] [17592186257106 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257108 13194139533864 true] [17592186257106 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257109 13194139533864 true] [17592186257106 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257110 13194139533864 true] [17592186257106 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257111 13194139533864 true] [17592186257106 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257112 13194139533864 true] [17592186257106 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257113 13194139533864 true] [17592186257106 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257114 13194139533864 true] [17592186257106 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533864 true] [17592186257106 1041 "selection" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257106 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257107 13194139533864 true] [17592186257106 1110 #uuid "6bf54287-4698-5a94-9cac-64d208e87386" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257107 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257107 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257107 1111 #uuid "6940f8b5-519f-52c4-bcac-f863b7c3b82e" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257108 1034 "II and III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257108 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257108 1111 #uuid "25867eeb-0029-578e-9ae6-86fdfc9f914d" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257109 1034 "I and III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592