#uuid "0fca9149-5777-5cb9-8cf8-a8c0ef67b2f0" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257624 1034 "I" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257624 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257624 1111 #uuid "3ba37a39-4d97-5b49-8d13-91ee55115a42" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257625 1034 "II, IV" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257625 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257625 1111 #uuid "6bb7170c-fa95-5385-bfd7-c1d6f7a4ff3a" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257626 1034 "I, IV" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257626 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257626 1111 #uuid "690893ff-0dc1-5c5a-8cdf-39aae72ff9e5" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257627 1034 "III, IV" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257627 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257627 1111 #uuid "cf9e1cb4-cca4-563d-bf5c-0dab612aa4b5" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257628 1034 "I, II" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257628 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257628 1111 #uuid "c6d5aea5-3dfa-517c-a044-6c722ffa4a07" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257629 1034 "I, II, IV" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257629 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257629 1111 #uuid "19be8788-5d4b-5792-b88b-d427cc1abe76" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257630 1034 "II, III, IV" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257630 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257630 1111 #uuid "845cd6bd-bf8f-56f6-b06a-250ba1f31627" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257631 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257632 13194139533864 true] [17592186257631 1089 "q-156162" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257631 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533864 true] [17592186257631 1100 "Given that ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is divergent, determine all real values of $K$ for which ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(K-3)\\cdot {a}_{n}$ is **convergent.**\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257631 1113 #uuid "6028f7b5-360d-5374-9eaf-4f3a559f7277" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257631 1145 "If we multiply the terms of a divergent series by a non-zero constant, the resulting series is divergent.\n\nHowever, multiplying the terms of a divergent series by $0$ gives a series that converges to $0.$\n\nTherefore, the series \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(K-3)\\cdot {a}_{n}\n$$\n\nis convergent when \n\n$$\nK-3=0\\,\\Rightarrow \\,K=3.\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257632 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257633 13194139533864 true] [17592186257632 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257632 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257632 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257633 13194139533864 true] [17592186257632 1110 #uuid "0aaf5648-6c39-5954-ba61-f78b65318168" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257633 1034 "3" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257633 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257633 1111 #uuid "d14ffde9-6472-5c5c-908f-3d98789b82d1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257634 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257635 13194139533864 true] [17592186257634 1089 "q-15640" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257634 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533864 true] [17592186257634 1100 "Consider the function $f(x)=3(x-2)^{3}$ and the point $P(3,3)$ that lies on $y=f(x).$ Given that $f(x)$ is invertible in the vicinity of $P,$  calculate ${({f}^{-1})}^{'}(3).$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257634 1113 #uuid "6fbbb0cf-47c7-5324-a25f-d63e213ac5e9" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257634 1145 "We start by calculating the derivative of $f$ at the point $(3,3).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =3(x-2)^{3} \\\\ {f}^{'}(x) & =9(x-2)^{2} \\\\ {f}^{'}(3) & =9\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $(3,3)$ lies on $y=f(x),$ we know that the corresponding point $(3,3)$ lies on $y={f}^{-1}(x).$\n\nFurthermore, the slopes of the tangents to the two respective points are reciprocals. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{({f}^{-1})}^{'}(3) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{'}({f}^{-1}(3))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{'}(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257635 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257636 13194139533864 true] [17592186257635 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257635 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257635 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257636 13194139533864 true] [17592186257635 1110 #uuid "a0ffa8c7-b03d-5de4-93f5-8a30fe004b83" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257636 1034 "\\frac{1}{9}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257636 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257636 1111 #uuid "2f6ccb33-929d-5295-997a-ab2f62a93871" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257637 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257638 13194139533864 true] [17592186257637 1089 "q-156739" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257637 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533864 true] [17592186257637 1100 "What is a horizontal asymptote of $y={log}_{8}x?$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}\n\nIf none exist, enter a phrase such as \"No horizontal asymptotes\"." 13194139533864 true] [17592186257637 1113 #uuid "bc9adfeb-d883-541f-9bc6-0ae368d34338" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257637 1145 "Let's recall the graph of $y={log}_{8}x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/import-ready/assets/c9bc40573836e39bfb5c9ea0dab41b66ba7bb753bc7580936a3eb206b968e5c1.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we note that for $x>1$, the graph grows very slowly as we increase $x.$ \n\nWe say that $y\\to \\infty $ (slowly) as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nTherefore, there are no horizontal asymptotes." 13194139533864 true] [17592186257638 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257639 13194139533864 true] [17592186257638 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257638 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257638 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257639 13194139533864 true] [17592186257638 1110 #uuid "989bc62c-f1d9-568f-95a9-4796196afea2" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257639 1034 "No horizontal asymptotes" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257639 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257639 1111 #uuid "e2a3223c-8742-53bd-8709-f6c1553158e7" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257640 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257641 13194139533864 true] [17592186257640 1089 "q-156741" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257640 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533864 true] [17592186257640 1100 "What is a horizontal asymptote of $y={log}_{6}x?$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}\n\nIf none exist, enter a phrase such as \"No horizontal asymptotes\"." 13194139533864 true] [17592186257640 1113 #uuid "d0452204-fefa-5ed6-b9ea-ca7949b58b72" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257640 1145 "Let's recall the graph of $y={log}_{6}x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/import-ready/assets/4177d9520b3758b29926eba7a7a74ed4c508d861e3c343f46c372ec79500fc9d.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we note that for $x>1$, the graph grows very slowly as we increase $x.$ \n\nWe say that $y\\to \\infty $ (slowly) as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nTherefore, there are no horizontal asymptotes." 13194139533864 true] [17592186257641 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257642 13194139533864 true] [17592186257641 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257641 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257641 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257642 13194139533864 true] [17592186257641 1110 #uuid "a156b458-fd69-567e-be85-623822c9cfeb" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257642 1034 "No horizontal asymptotes" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257642 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257642 1111 #uuid "a943c892-3b5f-5717-b297-77d4278d417c" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257643 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257644 13194139533864 true] [17592186257643 1089 "q-156743" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257643 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533864 true] [17592186257643 1100 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y={log}_{6}x?$ \n\nI. - It has no zeros\nII. - $y\\to 6$ as $x\\to \\infty $\nIII. - It has a vertical asymptote at $x=0$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257643 1113 #uuid "fde27731-67b5-58df-9931-b7a1dd7d4277" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257643 1145 "Let's plot the graph of $y={log}_{6}x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/import-ready/assets/d8d3f9dc995d8801d451b15129860362efa772178cdc3ef07be5adb6a1da5c45.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function has a zero at $x=1.$\n\n- Statement II is false. As $x$ increases, $y$ increases without bound. Therefore, $y\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty $\n\n- Statement III is true.\n\nIn conclusion, only statement III is true." 13194139533864 true] [17592186257644 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257645 13194139533864 true] [17592186257644 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257646 13194139533864 true] [17592186257644 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257647 13194139533864 true] [17592186257644 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257648 13194139533864 true] [17592186257644 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257649 13194139533864 true] [17592186257644 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257650 13194139533864 true] [17592186257644 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257651 13194139533864 true] [17592186257644 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257652 13194139533864 true] [17592186257644 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533864 true] [17592186257644 1041 "selection" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257644 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257649 13194139533864 true] [17592186257644 1110 #uuid "0dc1a05f-0f59-55a8-ba28-ee76724d625c" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257645 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257645 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257645 1111 #uuid "0c449a5c-9956-5c45-bb3f-1595038ff2e9" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257646 1034 "II and III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257646 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186257646 1111 #uuid "2fa5e593-c292-526d-965e-73cca1ddab4d" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257647 1034 "I and III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257647 1