-1)\\cdot {a}_{n}\n$$\n\nis convergent when\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{K}{2}-1 & =0 \\\\ \\frac{K}{2} & =1 \\\\ K & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257654 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257655 13194139533864 true] [17592186257654 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257654 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257654 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257655 13194139533864 true] [17592186257654 1110 #uuid "c2d6360e-374c-5656-a211-5ddc29753536" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257655 1034 "2" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257655 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257655 1111 #uuid "f081fa25-f9ba-5f97-b23b-48406f2126a3" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257656 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257657 13194139533864 true] [17592186257656 1089 "q-157060" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257656 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533864 true] [17592186257656 1100 "Given that ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent, which of the following is true regarding the series ${\\sum }_{n=85}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}?$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257656 1113 #uuid "11a1973e-aa91-5290-99cf-1bd17e28a67e" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257656 1145 "Removing the first $k-1$ terms from a convergent series results in a convergent series.\n\nMore precisely, assume that $k\\ge 1$ is an integer. Then, we have the following:\n\n*If ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent, then ${\\sum }_{n=k}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is also convergent.*\n\nSo, since ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent, we have that ${\\sum }_{n=85}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is also convergent." 13194139533864 true] [17592186257657 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257658 13194139533864 true] [17592186257657 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257659 13194139533864 true] [17592186257657 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533864 true] [17592186257657 1041 "selection" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257657 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257659 13194139533864 true] [17592186257657 1110 #uuid "9a1e69e2-802e-563b-bdb3