86257684 1089 "q-157096" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257684 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186257684 1100 "Given that ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent and ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is convergent, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. - ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is convergent\nII. - $-9\\cdot {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent\nIII. - ${\\sum }_{n=15}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is convergent" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257684 1113 #uuid "294c68f1-5d11-5151-93f2-31f75aac6241" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257684 1145 "Let's recall the properties of convergent series:\n\n- If ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent, then ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }K\\cdot {a}_{n}=K\\cdot {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is also convergent.\n\n- If ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent and ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is convergent, then ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is convergent.\n\n- If ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent, then ${\\sum }_{n=k}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is also convergent.\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. The sum of two convergent series is convergent.\n\n- Statement II is true. Any constant multiple of a convergent series gives a convergent series.\n\n- Statement III is true. Removing a finite number of terms from a convergent series gives a convergent series.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257685 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257686 13194139533864 true] [17592186257685 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257687 13194139533864 true] [17592186257685 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257688 13194139533864 true] [17592186257685 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257689 13194139533864 true] [17592186257685 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257690 13194139533864 true] [17592186257685 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257691 13194139533864 true] [17592186257685 1