11 #uuid "47cf5ddd-aac8-54a6-9cf6-8ff9e25b3283" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257694 1017 #edb/ref 17592186257695 13194139533864 true] [17592186257694 1089 "q-157099" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257694 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186257694 1100 "Given that ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent and ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is convergent, which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. - $11\\cdot {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent\nII. - ${\\sum }_{n=16}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is convergent\nIII. - $11\\cdot {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}+{\\sum }_{n=16}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is convergent" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257694 1113 #uuid "4e9d21a6-895c-56ef-b36c-707b55ffc68e" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257694 1145 "Let's recall the properties of convergent series:\n\n- If ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent, then ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }K\\cdot {a}_{n}=K\\cdot {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is also convergent.\n\n- If ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent and ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is convergent, then ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}$ is convergent.\n\n- If ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is convergent, then ${\\sum }_{n=k}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}$ is also convergent.\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true. Any constant multiple of a convergent series gives a convergent series.\n\n- Statement II is true. Removing a finite number of terms from a convergent series gives a convergent series.\n\n- Statement III is true. The sum of two convergent series is convergent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257695 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257696 13194139533864 true] [17592186257695 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257697 13194139533864 true] [17592186257695 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257698 13194139533864 true] [17592186257695 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257699 13194139533864 tru