, the combined transformation maps the local maximum of $y=f(x)$ to the local maximum of $y=3f(\\frac{x}{2}).$ So, we need to find the image of $(-2,-1),$ the local maximum of $y=f(x),$ under the transformation. \n\nTo plot $y=3f(\\frac{x}{2}),$ we apply the following steps: \n\n- First, we take the graph $y=f(x)$ that passes through $(-2,-1).$\n\n- Then, we  stretch the graph  along the $x$-axis by a scale factor of $2$ and get the graph of $y=f(\\frac{x}{2}).$ After this transformation, the point $(-2,-1)$ will be mapped to the point\n\n$$\n(2\\cdot (-2),-1)=(-4,-1).\n$$\n\n- Finally, we stretch the result  along the $y$-axis by a scale factor of $3$ and get the graph of $y=3f(\\frac{x}{2}).$ After this transformation, the point $(-4,-1)$ will be mapped to the point\n\n$$\n(-4,3\\cdot (-1))=(-4,-3).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the local maximum of $y=3f(\\frac{x}{2})$ is $(-4,-3).$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257923 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257924 13194139533864 true] [17592186257923 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257923 1041 "coordinate-1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257923 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257924 13194139533864 true] [17592186257923 1110 #uuid "7886f806-4b4e-5ec7-9ff0-f5abc6c38247" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257924 1034 "-4" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257924 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257924 1111 #uuid "c37f8b76-b2a0-54d0-81ef-dc0d585b9280" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257925 1000 #edb/ref 17592186257926 13194139533864 true] [17592186257925 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186257925 1041 "coordinate-2" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257925 1104 #edb/ref 17592186257926 13194139533864 true] [17592186257925 1110 #uuid "18331c92-2d7a-5990-b3ed-933af437497e" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257926 1034 "-3" 13194139533864 true] [17592186257926 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186257926 1111 #uuid "25a0f757-7428-5a0c-9bb3-857b616e17c0" 13194139533864 true] [175921