ormal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{'} & =-\\frac{1}{m} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258511 1000 #edb/ref 17592186258512 13194139533864 true] [17592186258511 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186258511 1041 "field-1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258511 1104 #edb/ref 17592186258512 13194139533864 true] [17592186258511 1110 #uuid "7f400028-7c20-514f-a009-3d6ef64a38fc" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258512 1034 "-\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258512 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186258512 1111 #uuid "1a79e81d-7957-5034-8f49-136ab4cac68c" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258513 1017 #edb/ref 17592186258514 13194139533864 true] [17592186258513 1089 "q-342152" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258513 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533864 true] [17592186258513 1100 "Find the slope ${m}^{'}$ of the normal line to the curve $y=2{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}$ at the point $(-1,-3).$\n\n${m}^{'}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258513 1113 #uuid "c5af5c6e-7b27-5022-a2e9-5d5ddf2fa935" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258513 1145 "Let $f(x)=2{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}.$ First, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{'}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{3}-{x}^{-4}) \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}+4{x}^{-5} \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}+\\frac{4}{{x}^{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the slope of the tangent at the point $(-1,-3):$\n\n$$\nm={f}^{'}(-1)=6{(-1)}^{2}+\\frac{4}{(-1)^{5}}=6-4=2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope ${m}^{'}$ of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{'} & =-\\frac{1}{m} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258514 1000 #edb/ref 17592186258515 13194139533864 true] [17592186258514 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186258514 1041 "field-1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258514 1104 #edb/ref 17592186258515 13194139533864 true] [17592186258514 1110 #uuid "46e92c24-80e6-5d0f-be8f-9482056003c8" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258515 1034 "-\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258515 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186258515 1111 #uuid "7bc826bc-caaa-5fab-8d91-1740d9955e1d" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258516 1017 #edb/ref 17592186258517 13194139533864 true] [17592186258516 1017 #edb/ref 17592186258519 13194139533864 true] [17592186258516 1089 "q-342163" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258516 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186258516 1100 "Find the equation of the normal line to the curve $y=4x-{x}^{3}$ at the point $(1,3).$\n\n$x\\,+$\n{{field-1}}$\\cdot \\,y\\,=$\n{{field-2}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258516 1113 #uuid "e1a6ea14-1871-540c-9817-e8bcb2170f98" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258516 1145 "Let $f(x)=4x-{x}^{3}.$ First, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\n{f}^{'}(x)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4x-{x}^{3})=4-3{x}^{2}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the slope of the tangent at the point $(1,3):$\n\n$$\nm={f}^{'}(1)=4-3({1}^{2})=1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the normal line is\n\n$$\n{m}^{'}=-\\frac{1}{m}=-1.\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-3 & =-1\\cdot (x-1) \\\\ y-3 & =-x+1 \\\\ x+1\\cdot y & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258517 1000 #edb/ref 17592186258518 13194139533864 true] [17592186258517 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186258517 1041 "field-1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258517 1104 #edb/ref 17592186258518 13194139533864 true] [17592186258517 1110 #uuid "08fbda2d-307a-5e11-987c-cf4a2e89319d" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258518 1034 "1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258518 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186258518 1111 #uuid "8ba24c34-cdde-566c-b78b-46a9c4176575" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258519 1000 #edb/ref 17592186258520 13194139533864 true] [17592186258519 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 131