0-b917-5f3f-8f89-44fd798a2554" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258593 1145 "Notice that the given series is a geometric series because the ratio of any two consecutive terms is constant.\n\nThe sum to infinity ${S}_{\\infty }$ of a geometric series is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{\\infty }=\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r},\\,|r|<1,\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term and $r$ is the common ratio.\n\nWe're told that the first term is\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=-7.\n$$\n\nThe common ratio is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{n+1}}{{a}_{n}}=0.5.\n$$\n\nSo, the sum of the series is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n} & =\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-7)}{(1-0.5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-7)}{(0.5)} \\\\  & =-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258594 1000 #edb/ref 17592186258595 13194139533864 true] [17592186258594 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186258594 1041 "field-1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258594 1104 #edb/ref 17592186258595 13194139533864 true] [17592186258594 1110 #uuid "30687167-a416-5b3d-a4e8-5eea820277d4" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258595 1034 "-14" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258595 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186258595 1111 #uuid "96f638d7-8251-569a-a6ec-34300fefaa66" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258596 1017 #edb/ref 17592186258597 13194139533864 true] [17592186258596 1089 "q-350576" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258596 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533864 true] [17592186258596 1100 "Given that ${a}_{1}=7$ and $\\frac{{a}_{n+1}}{{a}_{n}}=-0.4$ for all integers $n\\ge 1,$ find the value of ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}.$\n\n${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258596 1113 #uuid "d2e44366-3661-52c4-bfa0-64b9706d86c5" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258596 1145 "Notice that the given series is a geometric series because the ratio of any two consecutive terms is constant.\n\nThe sum to infinity ${S}_{\\infty }$ of a geometric series is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{\\infty }=\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r},\\,|r|<1,\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term and $r$ is the common ratio.\n\nWe're told that the first term is\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=7.\n$$\n\nThe common ratio is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{n+1}}{{a}_{n}}=-0.4.\n$$\n\nSo, the sum of the series is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n} & =\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{(1-(-0.4))} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{(1+0.4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{1.4} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258597 1000 #edb/ref 17592186258598 13194139533864 true] [17592186258597 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186258597 1041 "field-1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258597 1104 #edb/ref 17592186258598 13194139533864 true] [17592186258597 1110 #uuid "1f56f715-e231-5fc2-8f7e-fd84242b7707" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258598 1034 "5" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258598 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186258598 1111 #uuid "b12c1066-af2f-5cfe-a611-8a4523274537" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258599 1017 #edb/ref 17592186258600 13194139533864 true] [17592186258599 1089 "q-350588" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258599 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533864 true] [17592186258599 1100 "Evaluate the following series. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }3{(0.2)}^{n}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258599 1113 #uuid "6f8f961d-0c12-55d8-a6b7-610d52702173" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258599 1145 "Notice that the given series is a geometric series because it is in the form\n$\\sum a{r}^{n}.$\n\nThe sum to infinity ${S}_{\\infty }$ of a geometric series is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{\\infty }=\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r},\\,|r|<1,\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term and $r$ is the common ratio.\n\nThe first term is\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=3{(0.2)}^{1}=0.6.\n$$\n\nThe common ratio is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{3{(0.2)}^{2}}{3{(0.2)}^{1}}=0.2.\n$$\n\nSo, the sum of the series is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }3{(0.2)}^{n} & =\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.6}{1-0.2} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.6}{0.8} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258600 1000 #edb/ref 17592186258601 13194139533864 true] [17592186258600 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186258600 1041 "field-1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258600 1104 #edb/ref 17592186258601 13194139533864 true] [17592186258600 1110 #uuid "8e54e373-cf38-5ad3-9996-f860bc1db291" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258601 1034 "\\frac{3}{4}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258601 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186258601 1111 #uuid "ba9cd8e5-27e2-58d9-8af9-f42c3800d9d6" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258602 1017 #edb/ref 17592186258603 13194139533864 true] [17592186258602 1089 "q-350592" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258602 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533864 true] [17592186258602 1100 "Evaluate the following series. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{7}{5}{(0.3)}^{n}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258602 1113 #uuid "ecd963bf-5bba-5df2-996d-756760d0d41a" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258602 1145 "Notice that the given series is a geometric series because it is in the form\n$\\sum a{r}^{n}.$\n\nThe sum to infinity ${S}_{\\infty }$ of a geometric series is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{\\infty }=\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r},\\,|r|<1,\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term and $r$ is the common ratio.\n\nThe first term is\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\frac{7}{5}{(0.3)}^{1}=0.42.\n$$\n\nThe common ratio is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{\\frac{7}{5}{(0.3)}^{2}}{\\frac{7}{5}{(0.3)}^{1}}=0.3.\n$$\n\nSo, the sum of the series is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{7}{5}{(0.3)}^{n} & =\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.42}{1-0.3} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.42}{0.7} \\\\  & =\\frac{42}{70} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258603 1000 #edb/ref 17592186258604 13194139533864 true] [17592186258603 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186258603 1041 "field-1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258603 1104 #edb/ref 17592186258604 13194139533864 true] [17592186258603 1110 #uuid "2b831cea-f9fe-5289-ab8e-950cf1dfb3ea" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258604 1034 "\\frac{3}{5}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258604 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186258604 1111 #uuid "72a09274-3b82-53bb-92cc-b7199d2b2359" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258605 1017 #edb/ref 17592186258606 13194139533864 true] [17592186258605 1089 "q-350593" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258605 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533864 true] [17592186258605 1100 "Evaluate the following series. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }6{(0.75)}^{n}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258605 1113 #uuid "2a570aa2-6317-52cf-88ac-f33d0dd4de74" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258605 1145 "Notice that the given series is a geometric series because it is in the form\n$\\sum a{r}^{n}.$\n\nThe sum to infinity ${S}_{\\infty }$ of a geometric series is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{\\infty }=\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r},\\,|r|<1,\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term and $r$ is the common ratio.\n\nThe first term is\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=6{(0.75)}^{1}=4.5.\n$$\n\nThe common ratio is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{6{(0.75)}^{2}}{6{(0.75)}^{1}}=0.75.\n$$\n\nSo, the sum of the series is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }6{(0.75)}^{n} & =\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{4.5}{1-0.75} \\\\  & =\\frac{4.5}{0.25} \\\\  & =\\frac{450}{25} \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258606 1000 #edb/ref 17592186258607 13194139533864 true] [17592186258606 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186258606 1041 "field-1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258606 1104 #edb/ref 17592186258607 13194139533864 true] [17592186258606 1110 #uuid "20d1584c-c343-5091-b5fb-8a3f42a0ea37" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258607 1034 "18" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258607 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186258607 1111 #uuid "f810e291-0c36-56a6-a2a9-94abdfc6f33f" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258608 1017 #edb/ref 17592186258609 13194139533864 true] [17592186258608 1089 "q-350620" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258608 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186258608 1100 "Evaluate the following series. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\sum }_{n=4}^{\\infty }\\frac{64}{9}{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{n}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258608 1113 #uuid "a590ae1b-a6f1-59bc-ae08-476c39ab9fd7" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258608 1145 "First, note that the index $n$ starts from $4.$ However, it is still a geometric series because it is in the form $\\sum a{r}^{n}.$ \n\nIn this case, the first term is ${a}_{4},$ and so the sum to infinity ${S}_{\\infty }$ of this geometric series is given by\n\n$$\n{S}_{\\infty }=\\frac{{a}_{4}}{1-r},\\,|r|<1.\n$$\n\nFor the first few terms, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{4} & =\\frac{64}{9}{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{4}=\\frac{1}{36} \\\\ {a}_{5} & =\\frac{64}{9}{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{5}=\\frac{1}{144}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe common ratio is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{5}}{{a}_{4}}=\\frac{(\\frac{1}{144})}{(\\frac{1}{36})}=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nSo, the sum of the series is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=4}^{\\infty }\\frac{64}{9}{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{n} & =\\frac{{a}_{4}}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{36})}{(1-\\frac{1}{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{36})}{(\\frac{3}{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{36}\\cdot \\frac{4}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{27}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258609 1000 #edb/ref 17592186258610 13194139533864 true] [17592186258609 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186258609 1041 "field-1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258609 1104 #edb/ref 17592186258610 13194139533864 true] [17592186258609 1110 #uuid "865a5466-9fc0-5e19-ac48-97dd76755a81" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258610 1034 "\\frac{1}{27}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258610 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186258610 1111 #uuid "c93478d7-5ad1-5168-bdbd-35f035c0cd48" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258611 1017 #edb/ref 17592186258612 13194139533864 true] [17592186258611 1089 "q-350633" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258611 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533864 true] [17592186258611 1100 "Evaluate the geometric series ${\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }25{(\\frac{3}{5})}^{n+1}.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }25{(\\frac{3}{5})}^{n+1}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258611 1113 #uuid "9a515033-9d33-5db6-a4a5-02cf6fa471fb" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258611 1145 "First, note that the index $n$ starts from $2,$ and so the sum to infinity ${S}_{\\infty }$ of this geometric series is given by\n\n$$\n{S}_{\\infty }=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{1-r},\\,|r|<1.\n$$\n\nComputing the first few terms, we get:\n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=25{(\\frac{3}{5})}^{2+1}=\\frac{27}{5}\n$$\n\n \n\n$$\n{a}_{3}=25{(\\frac{3}{5})}^{3+1}=\\frac{81}{25}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the common ratio is \n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{3}}{{a}_{2}}=\\frac{(\\frac{81}{25})}{(\\frac{27}{5})}=\\frac{3}{5}.\n$$\n\nSo, the sum of the series is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }25{(\\frac{3}{5})}^{n+1} & =\\frac{{a}_{2}}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{27}{5})}{(1-\\frac{3}{5})} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{27}{5})}{(\\frac{2}{5})} \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258612 1000 #edb/ref 17592186258613 13194139533864 true] [17592186258612 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186258612 1041 "field-1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258612 1104 #edb/ref 17592186258613 13194139533864 true] [17592186258612 1110 #uuid "fb6c0036-bfd5-5b86-9819-1c43e8908c53" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258613 1034 "\\frac{27}{2}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186258613 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 tru