ng conditions must hold:\n\n- The reflected point $(b,a)$ must lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}x.$\n\n- The $y$-value of the point must lie in the range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}x,$ which is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of the points.  \n\n- First,  we consider the point $(\\sqrt{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\sqrt{3})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}x$ is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ and $y=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(\\sqrt{3},\\frac{\\pi }{3})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}x.$\n\n- Next, we consider the point $(\\sqrt{3},\\frac{\\pi }{4}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\sqrt{3})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}x.$ $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the point $(\\sqrt{3},\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}x.$\n\n- Finally, we consider the point $(\\sqrt{3},-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(-\\frac{2\\pi }{3},\\sqrt{3})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}x$ is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ and $y=-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ does **not** lie within this range. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the point $(\\sqrt{3},-\\frac{2\\pi }{3})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}x.$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259247 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259248 13194139533864 true] [17592186259247 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259249 13194139533864 true] [17592186259247 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259250 13194139533864 true] [17592186259247 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259251 13194139533864 true] [17592186259247 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259252 13194139533864 true] [17592186259247 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259253 13194139533864 true] [17592186259247 1000 #edb/