13194139533864 true] [17592186259345 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259349 13194139533864 true] [17592186259345 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259350 13194139533864 true] [17592186259345 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533864 true] [17592186259345 1041 "selection" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259345 1104 #edb/ref 17592186259346 13194139533864 true] [17592186259345 1110 #uuid "76679ae7-e49f-5cfc-8ca8-3a7fd4cd9d1b" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259346 1034 "\\frac{1}{k+2}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259346 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186259346 1111 #uuid "54cba1dc-4159-563c-8499-4148232d8332" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259347 1034 "k+1" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259347 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186259347 1111 #uuid "de83739b-023b-5227-b44f-ca056e1dbdd2" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259348 1034 "\\frac{k}{k+2}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259348 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186259348 1111 #uuid "9d922172-545f-554c-ab17-780785872aa2" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259349 1034 "\\frac{1}{{k}^{2}+2k}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259349 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186259349 1111 #uuid "310e603e-da3b-53ef-90e9-02dcb8cd7d8a" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259350 1034 "{k}^{2}+k" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259350 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186259350 1111 #uuid "2eff115d-21cd-5dde-aead-c1bd60d4224c" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259351 1017 #edb/ref 17592186259352 13194139533864 true] [17592186259351 1089 "q-73089" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259351 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533864 true] [17592186259351 1100 "If $f(x)$ is right-continuous at $x=-2$ and ${lim}_{x\\to (-2)^{+}}f(x)=-3,$ then what is \n${lim}_{x\\to (-2)^{+}}(3f(x)-xf(-2))?$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259351 1113 #uuid "ea15e55a-a35a-5c10-bdf0-ec97611a9f66" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259351 1145 "Since $f(x)$ is right-continuous at $x=-2,$ we must have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-2)^{+}}f(x)=f(-2)=-3.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-2)^{+}}(3f(x)-xf(-2)) & =3{lim}_{x\\to (-2)^{+}}f(x)-f(-2){lim}_{x\\to (-2)^{+}}x \\\\  & =3(-3)-(-3)(-2) \\\\  & =-15.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259352 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259353 13194139533864 true] [17592186259352 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186259352 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259352 1104 #edb/ref 17592186259353 13194139533864 true] [17592186259352 1110 #uuid "702438a2-1245-5baf-b9c4-4862b080363d" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259353 1034 "-15" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259353 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186259353 1111 #uuid "57d3e569-06f6-58e8-aae2-5751f55f7420" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259354 1017 #edb/ref 17592186259355 13194139533864 true] [17592186259354 1089 "q-73107" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259354 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186259354 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/import-ready/assets/88ea6a8d8a41b75aa433a17a2d861d32cf5f9eeb8e4c0995ef1eca2d12d1107a.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\nI. - The function is left-continuous at $x=-1$\nII. - The function is right-continuous at $x=-1$\nIII. - The function is continuous at $x=-1$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259354 1113 #uuid "84a6a876-1976-59db-8f65-20eb371fea76" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259354 1145 "Let's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. The function is left-continuous at $x=-1,$ since the left-sided limit is equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}f(x)=1=f(-1)\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. The function is not right-continuous at $x=-1,$ since the right-sided limit is not equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{+}}f(x)=2\\ne 1=f(-1)\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. In order for the function to be continuous at $x=-1,$ it must be both left-continuous and right-continuous. However, we have already determined that the function is not right-continuous at this point.\n\nIn conclusion, only statement I is true." 13194139533864 true] [17592186259355 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259356 13194139533864 true] [17592186259355 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259357 13194139533864 true] [17592186259355 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259358 13194139533864 true] [17592186259355 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259359 13194139533864 true] [17592186259355 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259360 13194139533864 true] [17592186259355 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259361 13194139533864 true] [17592186259355 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259362 13194139533864 true] [17592186259355 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259363 13194139533864 true] [17592186259355 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533864 true] [17592186259355 1041 "selection" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259355 1104 #edb/ref 17592186259359 13194139533864 true] [17592186259355 1110 #uuid "84eb593b-47ff-5268-873f-c5469234754a" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259356 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259356 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186259356 1111 #uuid "d0de8387-ae02-526f-b0ca-b74ec559a30c" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259357 1034 "II and III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259357 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186259357 1111 #uuid "e40a572c-ac4f-5b4b-84d3-99aa346437af" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259358 1034 "I and III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259358 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186259358 1111 #uuid "4c0ed898-69b9-5099-a484-f83f39fa809d" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259359 1034 "I only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259359 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186259359 1111 #uuid "b038d3d7-d0e5-5c15-8b4d-e053a3e14ab7" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259360 1034 "III only" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259360 11