cda033c" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259563 1017 #edb/ref 17592186259564 13194139533864 true] [17592186259563 1089 "q-81428" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259563 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533864 true] [17592186259563 1100 "Use the $p$-test to determine whether the series below converges or diverges.\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{8}{n}\n$$\n\nAnswer: {{answer}}" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259563 1113 #uuid "cf874b53-ef0a-5fdf-9ef3-0a8f809bc7de" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259563 1145 "The series can be written as\n\n$$\n8{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{n}.\n$$\n\nThis is a $p$-series with $p=1$ (the harmonic series). Since $p\\le 1,$ the series is divergent.\n\nNote that the factor of $8$ multiplying the series has no effect on the convergence/divergence of the series." 13194139533864 true] [17592186259564 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259565 13194139533864 true] [17592186259564 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533864 true] [17592186259564 1041 "answer" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259564 1104 #edb/ref 17592186259565 13194139533864 true] [17592186259564 1110 #uuid "38656401-8add-54f7-bee5-27e9e0e46e34" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259565 1034 "8" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259565 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533864 true] [17592186259565 1111 #uuid "fdf7ece4-2637-5e3a-b02a-bb98b44fc983" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259566 1017 #edb/ref 17592186259567 13194139533864 true] [17592186259566 1089 "q-81430" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259566 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533864 true] [17592186259566 1100 "Which of the following series converge?\n\nI. - ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{n}^{3}}}$\nII. - ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt[4]{{n}^{5}}}$\nIII. - ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{n}{\\sqrt{{n}^{3}}}$" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259566 1113 #uuid "9f47715f-32fb-5b55-bda6-7c06af34e3a5" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259566 1145 "We analyze each series in turn.\n\n- First, we look at ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{n}^{3}}}.$ Rewriting this gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{n}^{3}}}={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{n}^{3/2}},\n$$\n\nand this is a $p$-series with $p=\\frac{3}{2}.$ Since $p>1,$ the series converges by the $p$-series test.\n\n- For the second series, we have\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt[4]{{n}^{5}}}=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{n}^{5/4}},\n$$\n\n \nwhich is a $p$-series with $p=\\frac{5}{4}.$ Since $p>1,$ the series converges by the $p$-series test.\n\n- For the third series, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{n}{\\sqrt{{n}^{3}}} & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{n}{{n}^{3/2}} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{n}^{1/2}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand this is a $p$-series with $p=\\frac{1}{2}.$ Since $p\\le 1,$ the series is divergent.\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." 13194139533864 true] [17592186259567 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259568 13194139533864 true] [17592186259567 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259569 13194139533864 true] [17592186259567 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259570 13194139533864 true] [17592186259567 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259571 13194139533864 true] [17592186259567 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259572 13194139533864 true] [17592186259567 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259573 13194139533864 true] [17592186259567 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259574 13194139533864 true] [17592186259567 1000 #edb/ref 17592186259575 13194139533864 true] [17592186259567 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533864 true] [17592186259567 1041 "selection" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259567 1104 #edb/ref 17592186259573 13194139533864 true] [17592186259567 1110 #uuid "a6c8bf6f-5303-5a12-a675-f73664df7044" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259568 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259568 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533864 true] [17592186259568 1111 #uuid "23d0168c-6ede-54fb-9652-f394884c4e7e" 13194139533864 true] [17592186259569 1034 "II and